WEBVTT

00:00.290 --> 00:01.991
♪ &lt;i>Men...&lt;/i> ♪

00:02.650 --> 00:05.485
I can't believe you've managed
to stay in this house.

00:05.486 --> 00:08.655
You're like
a human barnacle.

00:08.656 --> 00:10.123
Thanks, Mom.

00:10.124 --> 00:12.092
Oh, I wasn't putting
you down, sweetheart.

00:12.093 --> 00:14.628
It's good that you have a skill.

00:14.629 --> 00:16.596
Did you come over for a reason,
or just to insult me?

00:16.597 --> 00:19.466
The two aren't
mutually exclusive.

00:19.467 --> 00:20.600
Mom.

00:20.601 --> 00:22.602
Charlie's bank
contacted me.

00:22.603 --> 00:25.672
Seems he had a secret
safe deposit box.

00:25.673 --> 00:28.642
I knew it! I knew he had to
have something squirreled away.

00:28.765 --> 00:31.034
Naturally, I went right
down there to check it out.

00:31.036 --> 00:32.819
So what was in it? Cash?
Diamonds? Krugerrands?

00:32.821 --> 00:34.787
Want to wipe your mouth?
You're drooling a little.

00:34.789 --> 00:36.206
Sorry.

00:36.208 --> 00:38.741
Actually, I was quite surprised
about what was in there.

00:38.743 --> 00:41.211
- Oh, tell me, tell me!
- I'll do better than that.

00:41.213 --> 00:42.745
Here.

00:42.747 --> 00:45.131
I'm pretty sure he
wanted you to have this.

00:46.568 --> 00:47.800
Oh boy, oh boy, oh boy...

00:47.802 --> 00:49.702
I knew you'd look out
for me, big bro.

00:49.704 --> 00:51.271
What the hell is this?

00:52.556 --> 00:53.806
Charlie's journal.

00:53.808 --> 00:54.974
Charlie kept a journal?

00:54.976 --> 00:57.543
Your brother was
a very complex man.

00:57.545 --> 00:59.812
Perhaps he needed a safe place

00:59.814 --> 01:02.815
to express his deepest emotions
and innermost thoughts,

01:02.817 --> 01:04.234
or some such nonsense.

01:05.769 --> 01:09.188
No. No cash, dear.
Already checked.

01:10.157 --> 01:11.441
Of course not.

01:11.443 --> 01:13.409
Why leave cash to your
impoverished brother

01:13.411 --> 01:16.663
when you can leave your
alcohol-muddled thoughts?

01:16.665 --> 01:18.364
Yay.

01:18.366 --> 01:21.284
"To whom it may concern,

01:21.286 --> 01:24.153
"if you are reading this it
means either my heart or lungs

01:24.155 --> 01:25.655
"finally gave out.

01:25.657 --> 01:27.657
"Or I rejected my new liver.

01:27.659 --> 01:31.827
"Or my brother wouldn't
give me a piece of his.

01:31.829 --> 01:33.846
"Or I choked on my own vomit,

01:33.848 --> 01:35.798
"or somebody else's.

01:35.800 --> 01:38.184
Or some crazy chick
pushed me in front of a bus..."

01:38.186 --> 01:40.002
Ooh, so close.

01:42.022 --> 01:46.342
Well, I hope reading it brings
you some comfort and closure.

01:46.344 --> 01:49.113
Are you sure that's all that
was in the safe deposit box?

01:49.114 --> 01:49.914
Yes.

01:49.939 --> 01:51.557
So my brother went
out to the bank

01:51.650 --> 01:54.033
and rented a safe deposit box
just for this journal?

01:54.035 --> 01:55.184
It would appear so.

01:55.186 --> 01:56.669
That makes no sense.

01:56.671 --> 01:58.321
He intimated on many occasions

01:58.323 --> 02:00.707
that he had some cash
stashed away for emergencies...

02:00.709 --> 02:04.327
you know, like getting
a hooker after an earthquake.

02:04.329 --> 02:08.131
Sweetheart, you have to
stop living in the past.

02:08.133 --> 02:09.966
What's done is done.

02:09.968 --> 02:11.851
Start looking forward.

02:11.853 --> 02:13.636
Yeah, I guess you're right.

02:13.638 --> 02:14.837
Is that a new watch?

02:14.839 --> 02:16.723
No.

02:16.725 --> 02:19.442
You have your whole
life ahead of you,

02:19.444 --> 02:23.446
and the fact is, you and I are
all that's left of this family.

02:23.448 --> 02:25.365
Well...

02:25.367 --> 02:27.150
you, me and Jake.

02:27.152 --> 02:29.168
Hey, Grandma.

02:30.405 --> 02:33.623
Whoa. Thought that was
coming out the other end.

02:36.076 --> 02:39.195
You're right.
It's just you and me.

02:39.197 --> 02:40.696
That looks like a man's Cartier.

02:40.698 --> 02:42.031
It's a knock-off.

02:43.167 --> 02:45.385
My point is,
with Charlie gone,

02:45.387 --> 02:48.171
you and I have to learn
how to help and support

02:48.173 --> 02:50.256
one another no matter what.

02:51.508 --> 02:54.227
Gee, that would be great.

02:54.229 --> 02:56.896
You were always
the good son.

02:58.015 --> 03:00.400
Now you're my only son.

03:01.602 --> 03:03.052
Oh, Mommy.

03:03.821 --> 03:06.022
Oh, Walden!
How nice to see you!

03:10.077 --> 03:12.445
It's a miracle
I'm not a transsexual

03:12.447 --> 03:15.064
on &lt;i>Dancing With the Stars.&lt;/i>

03:15.066 --> 03:17.900
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

03:17.902 --> 03:21.120
♪ Men, men, men, manly men, men, men ♪
♪ Ooh ♪

03:21.122 --> 03:24.340
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men ♪
♪ Ooh ♪

03:24.342 --> 03:26.426
♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh,
ooh-ohh, ooh-ooh... ♪

03:26.428 --> 03:28.928
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

03:28.930 --> 03:31.964
♪ Ooh ♪
♪ Men, men, men,  manly men, men, men ♪

03:31.966 --> 03:37.019
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

03:37.044 --> 03:40.144
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 9x07 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Those Fancy Japanese Toilets&lt;/font>
