03:40.145 --> 03:43.245
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

03:43.252 --> 03:45.703
I must tell you, Walden,
it's so nice to finally

03:45.705 --> 03:46.888
see someone in this house

03:46.890 --> 03:49.841
who surfs for something
other than porn.

03:49.843 --> 03:52.310
Yeah, I love the ocean.

03:52.312 --> 03:54.629
Just you alone with
your thoughts.

03:54.631 --> 03:58.249
Time standing still, at peace
with the entire universe.

03:58.251 --> 04:01.085
Plus, you can pee in it
and nobody knows.

04:01.087 --> 04:02.753
Charming.

04:02.755 --> 04:04.889
Actually, I'm glad
you stopped by.

04:04.891 --> 04:07.758
Um... Do you know a good
interior designer?

04:07.760 --> 04:11.613
As a matter of fact,
I know a great one.

04:14.266 --> 04:16.934
Evelyn Harper Interior Design.

04:16.936 --> 04:18.620
I thought you were
a real estate agent.

04:18.622 --> 04:21.072
I am. I'm also
a building inspector,

04:21.074 --> 04:24.209
mortgage broker, notary
public and a bail bondsman.

04:24.877 --> 04:26.244
A bail bondsman?

04:26.246 --> 04:29.547
Admittedly, that business has
slowed down since my son died.

04:29.549 --> 04:32.167
But getting back to your needs,

04:32.169 --> 04:35.136
what did you have in mind
in terms of redecorating?

04:35.138 --> 04:36.621
I don't know.

04:36.623 --> 04:39.507
I just, I just want my home
to reflect who I am.

04:39.509 --> 04:41.959
And who are you?

04:41.961 --> 04:45.963
I've got a buttload of money,
but I'm a pretty simple guy.

04:45.965 --> 04:49.734
I... like people, but
I don't entertain a lot.

04:49.736 --> 04:53.354
Oh, I'm not a neat freak,
but I don't like clutter.

04:53.356 --> 04:55.806
Oh, you know, and the most
important thing is,

04:55.808 --> 04:57.975
I want the house to use
green renewable energy,

04:57.977 --> 04:59.744
you know, like solar
power and wind power...

04:59.746 --> 05:01.946
Unless Brookstone or
somebody comes out with

05:01.948 --> 05:03.915
a home nuclear reactor,
because, I mean, come on,

05:03.917 --> 05:05.149
who wouldn't want one of those?

05:05.151 --> 05:08.953
"A buttload of money""

05:10.923 --> 05:12.340
You're in good hands.

05:16.462 --> 05:18.680
This journal is unbelievable.

05:18.682 --> 05:20.515
You aren't thinking of
publishing it, are you?

05:20.517 --> 05:22.767
What? Of course not, why?

05:22.769 --> 05:26.221
Well, I'm shoppin' around
my own Charlie memoir.

05:26.223 --> 05:29.507
It's called &lt;i>Man Whore.&lt;/i>

05:29.509 --> 05:31.893
It's catchy.

05:31.895 --> 05:34.028
But there was more to
Charlie than we thought.

05:34.030 --> 05:35.196
I mean, listen to this.

05:35.198 --> 05:38.650
"I just sent a girl home
who told me she loved me

05:38.652 --> 05:40.568
"and I can't even
remember her name.

05:40.570 --> 05:42.487
"What is wrong with me
that I just have

05:42.489 --> 05:44.405
"anonymous drunken encounters
night after night?

05:44.407 --> 05:46.157
"Do I drink to fill
the loneliness,

05:46.159 --> 05:49.827
or to hide from the
horror I've become?"

05:49.829 --> 05:52.630
You know, I feel awful that
I lived with him for so long

05:52.632 --> 05:54.132
and I didn't recognize his pain.

05:55.634 --> 05:57.719
"I remember, her name is Rachel!

05:57.721 --> 05:59.921
"I feel better now.

06:02.191 --> 06:05.593
I'll reward myself with some
cocaine and an Asian hooker."

06:08.480 --> 06:11.232
So remember, the key to
balancing the equation

06:11.234 --> 06:13.268
is to place coefficients
in front of each reactant

06:13.270 --> 06:15.603
and product so that
all the atoms balance.

06:17.107 --> 06:19.824
I bet you shower every day.

06:21.560 --> 06:23.060
Jake, we're supposed
to be studying

06:23.062 --> 06:24.162
for the chemistry mid-term.

06:24.164 --> 06:26.331
I'd rather study our chemistry.

06:26.333 --> 06:28.249
Lame.

06:28.251 --> 06:31.286
Really? I thought it
was a "double intendo."

06:32.705 --> 06:34.255
Hey, guys.

06:34.257 --> 06:36.040
Whatcha studying?

06:36.042 --> 06:37.625
Chemistry.

06:37.627 --> 06:39.410
Cool.

06:39.412 --> 06:42.046
Looks like you two
have a little chemistry.

06:43.266 --> 06:44.966
That's so clever.

06:47.770 --> 06:49.270
I'm Megan.

06:49.272 --> 06:51.639
Oh, hi, Megan. It's nice
to meet you. I'm Walden.

06:51.641 --> 06:53.941
Oh, are you the Walden
that bought the house?

06:53.943 --> 06:56.394
Yeah, how many Waldens
have you met lately?

06:56.396 --> 06:58.929
That's... that's so funny.

06:58.931 --> 07:01.616
And I'm lame.

07:01.618 --> 07:03.934
Well, it was nice to meet you.

07:03.936 --> 07:07.104
I'll let you guys get
back to your "chemistry."

07:07.106 --> 07:09.657
Bye, Walden!
It was nice meeting you too.

07:11.276 --> 07:15.380
You know, if he hooks up
with you, he goes to jail.

07:16.415 --> 07:18.466
I'd wait for him.

07:23.839 --> 07:28.176
"Peed blood again this morning.

07:28.178 --> 07:30.795
&lt;i>Should I be worried?"&lt;/i>

07:31.296 --> 07:33.464
As it turns out, no.

07:39.521 --> 07:43.241
We have to get
rid of Walden.

07:43.243 --> 07:46.143
- We do?
- Oh yeah, he's gotta go.

07:46.145 --> 07:48.329
Does it occur to you
that this is his house

07:48.331 --> 07:50.732
and if anybody goes,
it's gonna be us?

07:50.734 --> 07:53.351
Actually, no.

07:53.353 --> 07:54.919
What's the problem?

07:54.921 --> 07:56.788
He's stealing my girlfriend.

07:56.790 --> 07:58.489
Wait, I thought
she was your tutor.

07:58.491 --> 08:00.792
Think about it, Dad.
Would I have asked for a tutor

08:00.794 --> 08:03.828
if I didn't have a... what do
you call it, interior motive?

08:09.568 --> 08:12.019
Go on.

08:12.021 --> 08:14.722
She's only interested in
glomming onto Walden.

08:14.724 --> 08:16.340
Well, if it makes
you feel any better,

08:16.342 --> 08:18.860
I think my own mother likes
him more than she likes me.

08:18.862 --> 08:21.062
Why would that
make me feel better?

08:22.898 --> 08:25.433
I honestly don't know.

08:27.437 --> 08:29.721
Is this what I have to
look forward to in life?

08:29.723 --> 08:31.589
Always losing girls to
smarter, better-looking men?

08:31.591 --> 08:33.124
Well, think of it this way:

08:33.126 --> 08:35.309
you're carrying on a
proud family tradition.

08:39.631 --> 08:40.948
Hello, dear.

08:40.950 --> 08:42.300
What's all this?

08:42.302 --> 08:43.301
Oh, didn't you know?

08:43.303 --> 08:46.254
I'm helping young
Thor redecorate.

08:46.256 --> 08:48.589
I hope that's
all you're doing.

08:48.591 --> 08:50.258
Whatever do you mean?

08:50.260 --> 08:52.209
He's tall, he's handsome,
he's vulnerable,

08:52.211 --> 08:54.095
and you're old enough
to be his ancestor.

08:55.230 --> 08:57.214
Relax, Alan.
The only thing I want

08:57.216 --> 08:59.650
to pull out of that boy's
pants is his wallet.

08:59.652 --> 09:01.018
You sure?

09:01.020 --> 09:04.272
Believe me, I have
no ulterior motive.

09:04.274 --> 09:06.574
I believe that's
"interior," Grandma.

09:08.160 --> 09:12.747
You really should get that boy a
unicycle and some juggling pins.

09:12.749 --> 09:14.582
Evelyn, cool, you're here.
Uh, could you come on up?

09:14.584 --> 09:16.751
There's some things I want
you to do in my bedroom.

09:18.170 --> 09:21.088
Give the customer
what he wants.

09:24.276 --> 09:27.428
Okay, to start with,

09:27.430 --> 09:30.581
I want grey Carrara
marble counters,

09:30.583 --> 09:31.916
a steam shower...

09:31.918 --> 09:35.186
oh, and can we get one of
those fancy Japanese toilets

09:35.188 --> 09:37.305
that sprays water and
cleans your tushie?

09:37.307 --> 09:38.556
With your money you could afford

09:38.558 --> 09:40.975
an actual Japanese
person to do it.

09:40.977 --> 09:43.728
See what you can find.

09:43.730 --> 09:46.898
Okay, in here, I would like
to replace the bed frame,

09:46.900 --> 09:48.866
the curtains, the dresser,

09:48.868 --> 09:50.368
the end tables and the lamps.

09:50.370 --> 09:51.586
All right.

09:51.588 --> 09:53.671
What would you like
to replace them with?

09:53.673 --> 09:55.423
Um...

09:55.425 --> 09:57.175
A cooler bed frame,

09:57.177 --> 09:59.210
cooler curtains, cooler dresser,

09:59.212 --> 10:01.963
cooler end tables
and cooler lamps.

10:01.965 --> 10:05.299
"Cooler." I'm on it.

10:05.301 --> 10:07.451
Uh, now, would you
like to repaint?

10:07.453 --> 10:09.220
Hey, can I have walls

10:09.222 --> 10:11.422
that change color
depending on my mood?

10:11.424 --> 10:13.457
No.

10:13.459 --> 10:14.792
But we could paint them white

10:14.794 --> 10:17.127
and get you an industrial
strength antidepressant.

10:17.129 --> 10:19.129
That will work too.

10:19.131 --> 10:20.848
Would you like to
keep the camera?

10:20.850 --> 10:22.783
What camera?

10:25.954 --> 10:27.522
Aw...

10:27.524 --> 10:29.139
Awesome!

10:29.141 --> 10:31.976
I'm on TV.

10:31.978 --> 10:33.244
Hello!

10:33.246 --> 10:36.146
I am so keeping that.

10:36.148 --> 10:37.949
All right. Anything else?

10:37.951 --> 10:41.586
Can I have a Jacuzzi
on the balcony?

10:41.588 --> 10:43.654
'Cause I'm single now,
so I'm going to be

10:43.656 --> 10:47.491
having sex with a lot of
women I haven't met yet.

10:47.493 --> 10:51.212
Oh... I just got an idea!

10:51.214 --> 10:56.050
Just out of curiosity, what kind
of woman are you attracted to?

10:56.052 --> 10:58.002
There's my wife.

10:58.004 --> 11:00.337
Oh, and there's women
who look like my wife.

11:00.339 --> 11:01.806
That's very romantic.

11:01.808 --> 11:03.474
Oh, and Ellen DeGeneres.

11:03.476 --> 11:04.775
I don't know
what it is.

11:04.777 --> 11:06.360
Whether it's the slacks
or the way she dances--

11:06.362 --> 11:08.029
it's hot.

11:08.031 --> 11:10.281
♪ Men. ♪

11:13.629 --> 11:15.445
♪ Men. ♪

11:17.782 --> 11:19.216
You're up early.

11:19.218 --> 11:21.385
Charlie's journal-- I
can't stop reading it.

11:21.387 --> 11:22.586
Listen to this.

11:22.588 --> 11:24.588
"My brother's kid
showed up today.

11:24.590 --> 11:26.089
"He's kind of cute.

11:26.091 --> 11:28.208
"No way he's really Alan's kid.

11:29.911 --> 11:32.312
"And best of all,
he's smart as a whip.

11:32.314 --> 11:35.515
I think he's got
a very bright future."

11:35.517 --> 11:38.352
Oh, that just
breaks my heart.

11:38.354 --> 11:39.486
Yeah.

11:39.488 --> 11:41.738
We were all so young
and naive then.

11:41.740 --> 11:42.906
Hey.

11:42.908 --> 11:45.809
Hey.

11:52.333 --> 11:54.584
What? I took a huge dump.

11:57.989 --> 12:00.757
No way he's really my kid.

12:05.997 --> 12:07.597
You look very pretty today.

12:07.599 --> 12:09.866
Jake, I'm here
to study.

12:09.868 --> 12:11.368
The test was yesterday.

12:11.370 --> 12:14.187
I already failed.

12:14.189 --> 12:15.288
Hey, guys.

12:15.290 --> 12:17.357
Hey, Walden.

12:17.359 --> 12:18.508
Here we go.

12:18.510 --> 12:22.612
Whoa, Megan,
you look very pretty today.

12:22.614 --> 12:23.847
Thanks.

12:23.849 --> 12:25.449
You look pretty, too.

12:26.868 --> 12:28.518
Thank you.

12:28.520 --> 12:29.853
Where are you going?

12:29.855 --> 12:33.206
Oh, I am going furniture
shopping with Jake's grandma.

12:33.208 --> 12:35.409
Oh, I love furniture.

12:36.544 --> 12:39.529
And grandmas.

12:39.531 --> 12:40.864
Cool.

12:42.250 --> 12:43.583
See ya.

12:43.585 --> 12:46.202
See ya.

12:46.204 --> 12:47.554
Okay, Megan,

12:47.556 --> 12:48.755
I know what's going on here

12:48.757 --> 12:50.841
and I really don't appreciate...

12:53.044 --> 12:54.144
What's that about?

12:54.146 --> 12:56.313
I don't know. I'm
just in the mood.

12:56.315 --> 12:57.514
Okay.

12:59.567 --> 13:01.051
Come on.

13:01.053 --> 13:02.569
Okay.

13:02.571 --> 13:03.603
Where are we going?

13:03.605 --> 13:04.905
To your room.

13:04.907 --> 13:07.107
Okay.

13:08.993 --> 13:12.395
Hello, gorgeous.

13:12.397 --> 13:14.414
Did you miss me?

13:14.416 --> 13:16.700
'Cause I sure missed you.

13:16.702 --> 13:19.953
Let me pull this thing
out of you.

13:31.200 --> 13:34.134
Are you gonna turn your car off?

13:36.472 --> 13:39.255
I did.

13:41.109 --> 13:43.193
Might need service.

13:43.195 --> 13:45.779
Sadly, that's where
I just came from.

13:49.935 --> 13:52.819
You know what's great
about my electric car?

13:52.821 --> 13:54.237
What?

13:55.207 --> 13:56.540
I just turned it on.

13:56.542 --> 13:58.308
Sweet.

13:58.310 --> 13:59.976
So where you headed?

13:59.978 --> 14:01.661
Um, I'm going
to pick up your mom.

14:01.663 --> 14:02.996
We're going furniture shopping.

14:02.998 --> 14:04.948
Okay, well, just
a little heads up

14:04.950 --> 14:07.951
before you journey to
the caves of Mordor.

14:07.953 --> 14:09.719
My mother has what
you might call

14:09.721 --> 14:12.172
a, uh, proclivity
for younger men.

14:12.174 --> 14:13.456
You mean she's like a cougar?

14:13.458 --> 14:15.458
No, she's not
"like a cougar""

14:15.460 --> 14:16.843
she's the mother
of all cougars.

14:16.845 --> 14:19.796
So kind of an uber-cougar?

14:19.798 --> 14:22.015
A super duper
uber-cougar.

14:22.017 --> 14:23.650
You think a bit of better butter

14:23.652 --> 14:25.852
would make
her bitter batter better?

14:25.854 --> 14:27.888
What?

14:27.890 --> 14:30.107
I just like saying that.

14:30.109 --> 14:31.458
Walden, I'm
serious here.

14:31.460 --> 14:33.026
Don't worry.

14:33.028 --> 14:34.661
I'm not going to hook up
with your mom.

14:34.663 --> 14:37.147
Yeah, if I had a dime for
every time I heard that,

14:37.149 --> 14:39.332
I'd have $3.60.

14:40.451 --> 14:42.536
And I know that doesn't
sound like a lot,

14:42.538 --> 14:44.955
but it is 36 times.

14:44.957 --> 14:47.908
That's a very weird thing
to keep track of.

14:47.910 --> 14:49.843
I got a lot
of free time.

14:49.845 --> 14:53.296
Trust me,
nothing's going to happen.

14:53.298 --> 14:56.166
Okay. But try not to
hurt her feelings.

14:56.168 --> 14:58.351
I mean, she may be a rapacious
sexual predator,

14:58.353 --> 15:00.720
but she breaks
just like a little girl.

15:00.722 --> 15:02.055
Understood.

15:02.057 --> 15:04.174
Oh, hey, check it out.

15:04.176 --> 15:06.276
I got voice control.

15:06.278 --> 15:07.861
Lights on.

15:09.847 --> 15:11.448
Radio on.

15:14.186 --> 15:15.869
Back up.

15:18.372 --> 15:20.373
Bye!

15:27.331 --> 15:31.201
Well, you may not be
pretty or expensive,

15:31.203 --> 15:33.803
but you get me
where I want to go.

15:38.392 --> 15:40.260
Thank you for walking
me to my door.

15:40.262 --> 15:42.145
You don't meet many
gentlemen nowadays.

15:42.147 --> 15:43.230
You're welcome.

15:43.232 --> 15:44.364
Is that a camera?

15:44.366 --> 15:46.316
Hello!

15:46.318 --> 15:49.352
Would you like to come in
for a drink before you go?

15:49.354 --> 15:52.105
I don't know,
I should probably get going.

15:52.107 --> 15:53.156
What's your hurry?

15:53.158 --> 15:54.774
I just think that

15:54.776 --> 15:56.776
we should keep
our relationship business

15:56.778 --> 15:59.946
and not "biznass."

15:59.948 --> 16:03.399
Oh, my goodness,
do you think I'm hitting on you?

16:04.452 --> 16:08.205
W-Well, Alan did say
that you're an uber-cougar.

16:08.207 --> 16:10.423
An uber-cougar?

16:10.425 --> 16:12.926
A super duper uber-cougar.

16:15.464 --> 16:17.297
Oh, my Lord.

16:17.299 --> 16:19.516
Now, you listen to me,
young man.

16:19.518 --> 16:22.519
My son has some serious issues.

16:22.521 --> 16:24.638
And he tends to imagine things.

16:24.640 --> 16:29.476
Believe me, I have no carnal
designs on you whatsoever.

16:29.478 --> 16:31.144
Really?

16:31.146 --> 16:35.115
For God's sake, Walden, I'm old
enough to be your mother.

16:35.117 --> 16:38.434
Assuming a teenage pregnancy
of course.

16:38.436 --> 16:40.737
Okay, sure.

16:40.739 --> 16:42.939
I'll have a drink.

16:55.620 --> 16:57.804
Are you going to tell Alan?

17:00.224 --> 17:03.960
I'm going to tell everyone.

17:03.962 --> 17:06.179
♪ Men. ♪

17:10.104 --> 17:12.104
♪ Men. ♪

17:12.130 --> 17:14.865
&lt;i>"Alan moved in with&lt;/i>
&lt;i>his girlfriend yesterday.&lt;/i>

17:14.867 --> 17:18.619
&lt;i>"How stupid is she?&lt;/i>

17:18.621 --> 17:20.204
&lt;i>"Oh, well, doesn't matter.&lt;/i>

17:20.206 --> 17:22.239
&lt;i>"Like a nonspecific&lt;/i>
&lt;i>urinary infection,&lt;/i>

17:22.241 --> 17:26.126
&lt;i>"I'm sure he'll be back&lt;/i>
&lt;i>before long.&lt;/i>

17:26.128 --> 17:28.212
&lt;i>"Truth be told,&lt;/i>
&lt;i>I actually kind of miss&lt;/i>

17:28.214 --> 17:30.497
&lt;i>"the jug-eared freeloader.&lt;/i>

17:30.499 --> 17:32.750
&lt;i>How stupid am I?"&lt;/i>

17:34.636 --> 17:37.371
I don't believe it.

17:37.373 --> 17:40.007
He loved me.

17:40.009 --> 17:42.209
My brother loved me.

17:45.096 --> 17:46.380
&lt;i>"Speaking of stupid,&lt;/i>

17:46.382 --> 17:48.732
&lt;i>"today I bought&lt;/i>
&lt;i>a $100,000 Cartier watch.&lt;/i>

17:48.734 --> 17:50.167
&lt;i>"But I'm afraid to wear it,&lt;/i>

17:50.169 --> 17:52.519
&lt;i>so I'm gonna keep it&lt;/i>
&lt;i>in my safe deposit box."&lt;/i>

17:52.521 --> 17:55.189
Son of a bitch!

17:55.191 --> 17:57.691
That was, that was great.

18:00.061 --> 18:01.078
Just-Just great.

18:01.080 --> 18:03.330
Thank you so much.

18:08.253 --> 18:09.653
Hey.

18:09.655 --> 18:11.689
Hey. How'd it go
with my mom?

18:11.691 --> 18:14.241
Fine, fine.

18:14.243 --> 18:16.543
Just shopped for furniture.

18:17.629 --> 18:21.515
Rugs, chairs and tables.

18:21.517 --> 18:23.267
Nice.

18:23.269 --> 18:25.886
Armoires, ottomans,

18:25.888 --> 18:27.855
curtains, recliners,

18:27.857 --> 18:30.291
love seats, throw pillows.

18:30.293 --> 18:32.476
Okay, good night.

18:34.312 --> 18:37.031
Oh, yeah, she did him.

18:37.033 --> 18:39.116
Bye. Thanks again!

18:39.118 --> 18:40.651
Hey, dude, how you doing?

18:40.653 --> 18:41.485
Fantastic.

18:41.487 --> 18:43.654
I love you, man.

18:46.374 --> 18:47.986
Thanks.

18:49.602 --> 18:51.338
What an affectionate family.

18:54.120 --> 18:58.120
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==
